ol_014: C4H7NO (4-aminobutanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C3H6O2 (propionic acid) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_004, mol_005, mol_002, mol_006 -> mol_011 (Strecker synthesis of glycine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_015, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_008 (Reductive amination forming \u03b3-aminobutyric acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_008 -> mol_009 (Lactamization to proline (non-selective cyclization)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_009 -> mol_010 (Pyrrolidine ring closure (enantioselective cyclization)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_005: mol_004, mol_005, mol_011, mol_002, mol_006 -> mol_012 (Successive Strecker elongation to aminopentanenitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_012, mol_006 -> mol_009 (Hydrolysis of Strecker adduct to proline (racemate)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_009 -> mol_010 (Partial resolution by chiral crystallization) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_005, mol_002 -> mol_014 (Amination and chain extension to 4-aminobutanal) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_014 -> mol_009 (Cyclization of 4-aminobutanal to proline) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_005, mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_013 (Reductive amination of propionaldehyde to 3-aminopropanal) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_013, mol_005, mol_002 -> mol_014 (Aldol extension and amination: 3-aminopropanal + formaldehyde) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_007, mol_005 -> mol_015 (Alanine aldol condensation to propanoic acid) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Hydrothermal amination route via \u03b3-aminobutyric acid (4 steps)\n  - P2: Strecker glycine homologation pathway (4 steps)\n  - P3: Formaldehyde chain extension via aminated aldehydes (4 steps)\n  - P4: Strecker route with partial chiral induction (4 steps)\n  - P5: Propanoic acid non-aminated route (4 steps)\n  - P6: Direct aldehyde build-up and cyclization (3 steps)\n  - P7: Hydrothermal chain via 3-aminopropanal extension (4 steps)\n  - P8: Successive Strecker with chiral crystallization (4 steps)\n  - P9: Direct amination of propanoic acid followed by lactamization (4 steps)\n  - P10: Aldehyde pathway using surface cycling and mineral promotion (3 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 12 reactions | 2 balanced as written | 0 balanceable with coefficients | 10 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: HCN + CH2O + NH3 + H2O -> C2H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C3H6O2 + NH3 + H2 -> C4H9NO2 | reactants minus products: C-1, H+2 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C4H9NO2 -> C5H9NO2 | reactants minus products: C-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: HCN + CH2O + C2H5NO2 + NH3 + H2O -> C5H10N2O2 | reactants minus products: C-1, H+3, N+1, O+2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as product\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C5H10N2O2 + H2O -> C5H9NO2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: CH2O + NH3 -> C4H7NO | reactants minus products: C-3, H-2 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_009 UNBALANCED: C4H7NO -> C5H9NO2 | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: CH2O + NH3 + H2 -> C3H7NO | reactants minus products: C-2 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product\n  - rxn_011 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO + CH2O + NH3 -> C4H7NO | reactants minus products: H+5, N+1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_012 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO2 + CH2O -> C3H6O2 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+3, N+1, O+1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\nFormula/structure inconsistencies:\n  - mol_009: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_010: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\nTreat this check as ground truth for mass and charge conservation. Reactions that cannot be balanced violate conservation: reflect this in chemical_feasibility and reaction_scores, list them in problematic_reactions, and name the specific reaction IDs (with the missing species, if hinted) in your feedback so the network can be corrected. Note that implausibly large inferred coefficients may also indicate a mis-specified reaction.\n=== END BALANCE CHECK ===\n\n\nPlease evaluate the network and respond with JSON:\n{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"<id>\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\"rxn_001\": 0.85, ...},\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"environmental_progression\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"target_achievement\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"feedback\": \"<pathway-specific feedback>\",\n            \"approved\": <true if confidence >= 0.8>,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_ids with issues\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\"improvements\"]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"best_pathway_id\": \"<id of best pathway>\",\n    \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n    \"network_feedback\": \"<overall assessment>\"\n}\n\nNote: \"environmental_progression\" scores Environmental Consistency (conditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_002\": 0.5,\n                \"rxn_003\": 0.4,\n                \"rxn_004\": 0.7\n      