m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Proline\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The network constructs L-proline from plausible prebiotic feedstocks via a diverse set of pathways: homologation, reductive amination, Strecker-type transformations, and surface-catalyzed cyclization, spanning hydrothermal, surface, and prebiotic microenvironment conditions. Each pathway is atom- and charge-balanced, with byproducts explicitly specified throughout. By leveraging C1 and C2 sources (HCN, glyoxylate, formaldehyde/acrolein, NH3, CO2), the network systematically builds the 5-membered pyrrolidine backbone and introduces chirality using plausible geochemical selectors.\n\nMOLECULES (18 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2O (water) [starting]\n  - mol_002: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_003: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_005: CH2O (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_006: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_007: C2H2O2 (glyoxylate) [starting]\n  - mol_008: C2H5NO2 (glycine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C4H9NO2 (\u03b3-aminobutyric acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C4H7NO2 (aminocrotonic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C5H9NO2 (L-Proline) [target]\n  - mol_013: C3H5NO (3-aminopropionaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: C4H7NO (4-aminobutanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: C3H6O (propanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C4H6O2 (maleic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C5H7NO2 (\u03941-pyrroline-2-carboxylic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_018: C3H7NO2 (DL-alanine) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (12 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_005, mol_006, mol_004, mol_001 -> mol_008, mol_001 (Glycine synthesis via Strecker reaction) [Surface]\n  - rxn_002: mol_008, mol_005 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Alanine synthesis from glyoxylate by homologation) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_009, mol_002 -> mol_013, mol_001 (Aminopropionaldehyde formation by reduction of alanine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_004: mol_013 -> mol_017 (Cyclization of 3-aminopropanal to pyrroline intermediate) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_005: mol_017, mol_002 -> mol_012 (Reduction of pyrroline-2-carboxylic acid to L-proline) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_006: mol_015, mol_006, mol_004, mol_001 -> mol_010, mol_001 (Strecker synthesis of \u03b3-aminobutyric acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_010 -> mol_011, mol_001 (Dehydration to aminocrotonic acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_011 -> mol_012 (Cyclization to proline (via aminocrotonic acid)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_009: mol_008, mol_016 -> mol_010, mol_003 (Glycine chain elongation via acrolein condensation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_015, mol_004 -> mol_014 (Amination of butanal to yield 4-aminobutanal) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_014, mol_003 -> mol_017, mol_001 (4-aminobutanal cyclization to \u03941-pyrroline-2-carboxylate) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_012: mol_007, mol_006, mol_004, mol_001 -> mol_018, mol_001 (Alternative Strecker synthesis yielding alanine) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Hydrothermal glycine\u2192alanine reduction/cyclization route (5 steps)\n  - P2: Surface Strecker \u03b3-aminobutyric acid (GABA) route (4 steps)\n  - P3: Direct Strecker \u03b3-aminobutyric acid/proline path (3 steps)\n  - P4: Reductive hydrothermal amination/cyclization pathway (4 steps)\n  - P5: Aldehyde amination/cyclization with hydrothermal CO2 (3 steps)\n  - P6: Alternative Strecker alanine/homologation route (4 steps)\n  - P7: Alanine\u2014>aminopropanal direct reduction route (4 steps)\n  - P8: Maleic acid chain extension pathway (3 steps)\n  - P9: Propanal-based amination/cyclization (3 steps)\n  - P10: Cyclization with exogenous CO2 (butanal amination) (3 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 12 reactions | 2 balanced as written | 1 balanceable with coefficients | 9 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: CH2O + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C2H5NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H+1, N+1, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C2H5NO2 + CH2O -> C3H7NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H-2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C3H7NO2 + H2 -> C3H5NO + H2O | reactants minus products: H+2 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: C3H5NO -> C5H7NO2 | reactants minus products: C-2, H-2, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_006 UNBALANCED: C3H6O + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C4H9NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H+1, N+1, O-1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_007 UNBALANCED: C4H9NO2 -> C4H7NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: O-1 | balanceable if adding: O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: C4H7NO2 -> C5H9NO2 | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_009 balanceable: C2H5NO2 + C4H6O2 -> C4H9NO2 + 2 CO2\n  - rxn_010 UNBALANCED: C3H6O + NH3 -> C4H7NO | reactants minus products: C-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_012 UNBALANCED: C2H2O2 + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C3H7NO2 + H2O | reactants minus products: H-1, N+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as reactant; CO2 as product; CO as product; HCN as product\nFormula/structure inconsistencies:\n  - mol_011: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_013: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\n  - mol_014 (4-aminobutanal): stated formula C4H7NO disagrees with its InChI structure (stated minus InChI: H-2)\n  - mol_016 (maleic acid): stated formula C4H6O2 disagrees with its InChI structure (stated minus InChI: H+2, O-2)\n  - mol_017: InChI could not be parsed by RDKit (RDKit could not parse InChI)\nTreat this check as ground truth for mass and charge conservation. Reactions that cannot be balanced violate conservation: reflect this in chemical_feasibility and reaction_scores, list them in problematic_reactions, and name the specific reaction IDs (with the missing species, if hinted) in your feedback so the network can be corrected. Note that implausibly large inferred coefficients may also indicate a mis-specified reaction.\n=== END BALANCE CHECK ===\n\n\nPlease evaluate the network and respond with JSON:\n{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"<id>\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\"rxn_001\": 0.85, ...},\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"environmental_progression\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"target_achievement\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n            \"feedback\": \"<pathway-specific feedback>\",\n            \"approved\": <true if confidence >= 0.8>,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_ids with issues\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\"improvements\"]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"best_pathway_id\": \"<id of best pathway>\",\n    \"overall_confidence\": <0.0-1.0>,\n    \"network_feedback\": \"<overall assessment>\"\n}\n\nNote: \"environmental_progression\" scores Environmental Consistency (conditions fit each\nreaction's stated environment), not any particular order of environments.\n", "raw_response": "{\n    \"pathway_evaluations\": [\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P1\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_001\": 0.6,\n                \"rxn_002\": 0.6,\n                \"rxn_003\": 0.6,\n                \"rxn_004\": 0.5,\n                \"rxn_005\": 0.9\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.58,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.7,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.68,\n            \"feedback\": \"P1 includes a series of unbalanced reactions (rxn_001\u2013rxn_004). Key intermediates are identified and the pathway is logical, but mass balance failures throughout (except rxn_005, which is reasonable) harm chemical feasibility. Environmental assignments largely make sense. Correction of atom balances and some mechanistic steps is needed.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Fix atom imbalances, specify byproducts.\",\n                \"Clarify cyclization step mechanism and conserve mass.\",\n                \"Check intermediate formulas for accuracy.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_006\": 0.6,\n                \"rxn_007\": 0.6,\n                \"rxn_008\": 0.5,\n                \"rxn_005\": 0.9\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.65,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.65,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0