m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Proline\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This network employs multiple convergent strategies characteristic of prebiotic chemistries: (1) hydrothermal and surface environments to generate 4-aminobutanoic acid (GABA) and its aldehyde/deaminated analogs; (2) Strecker-like homologation, reductive amination, and multistep chain extension to reach the C4-amine backbone; (3) mineral surface catalysis, especially by iron sulfides and clays, to promote carbon-nitrogen bond formation and ring closure; (4) ring-closing lactam cyclizations under dehydration conditions to yield proline. Mechanistically, the network is built around well-supported transformations (Strecker synthesis, reductive amination, hydrothermal carbonyl chemistry, and surface-facilitated cyclizations), arranged in ten distinct yet intersecting pathways to maximize chemical plausibility and atom balance.\n\nMOLECULES (17 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2CO (formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_002: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_003: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: C2H5NO2 (glycine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: C3H7NO2 (alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_006: C3H7NO (3-aminopropanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C4H9NO2 (GABA) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C4H7NO2 (4-aminobut-2-enoic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C4H7NO (4-aminobutanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C5H9NO2 (L-proline) [target]\n  - mol_011: CO (carbon monoxide) [starting]\n  - mol_012: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_013: C3H6O (propanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_015: H2O (water) [intermediate]\n  - mol_016: C4H7NO2 (DL-proline (racemic)) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C4H8O2 (butyric acid) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (16 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_003, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_004 (Strecker synthesis of glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_004, mol_001, mol_003, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_005 (Amino acid chain extension via aldehyde and Strecker homologation) [Surface]\n  - rxn_003: mol_013, mol_002 -> mol_005 (Transamination of propanal to alanine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_004: mol_013, mol_002, mol_014 -> mol_006, mol_015 (Reductive amination of propanal to 3-aminopropanal) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_005: mol_017, mol_002, mol_014 -> mol_007, mol_015 (Amination of butanoic acid to 4-aminobutanoic acid (GABA)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_006: mol_013, mol_001, mol_012, mol_015 -> mol_017 (Aldol extension of propanal to butanoic acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_007: mol_006, mol_012, mol_015 -> mol_007 (Oxidation of 3-aminopropanal to GABA) [Surface]\n  - rxn_008: mol_007 -> mol_010, mol_015 (Dehydration cyclization of GABA to proline (lactamization)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_007 -> mol_008, mol_014 (Dehydrogenation of GABA to 4-aminobut-2-enoic acid) [Surface]\n  - rxn_010: mol_008, mol_015 -> mol_010, mol_014 (Cyclization of 4-aminobut-2-enoic acid to proline (unsaturated route)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_011: mol_005, mol_012, mol_015 -> mol_013, mol_002 (Oxidative deamination of alanine to propanal) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_009 -> mol_010 (Cyclization of 4-aminobutanal to proline (direct cyclization)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_013: mol_009, mol_012 -> mol_007, mol_015 (Oxidation of 4-aminobutanol to GABA) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_004, mol_001, mol_003, mol_002, mol_015 -> mol_007 (Homo-Strecker homologation (GABA from glycine via C2 extension)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_015: mol_007 -> mol_016, mol_015 (Racemic proline generation via non-selective lactamization) [Surface]\n  - rxn_016: mol_016 -> mol_010 (Chiral resolution of DL-proline) [Biochemical]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: GABA route via aldehyde amination and cyclization (6 steps)\n  - P2: Butanoic acid amination pathway (6 steps)\n  - P3: Direct cyclization of aminoaldehyde pathway (3 steps)\n  - P4: Unsaturated GABA and cyclization (3 steps)\n  - P5: Double Strecker homologation to GABA, then proline (3 steps)\n  - P6: Racemic proline and chiral resolution (4 steps)\n  - P7: Oxidative conversion of aminoaldehyde to GABA, then proline (4 steps)\n  - P8: Transamination-oxidation to propanal pathway (6 steps)\n  - P9: Chain-elongation via surface-catalyzed Strecker (3 steps)\n  - P10: Silica-catalyzed DL-proline with chiral enrichment (2 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 16 reactions | 1 balanced as written | 1 balanceable with coefficients | 14 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 UNBALANCED: H2CO + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C2H5NO2 | reactants minus products: H+3, N+1 | balanceable if adding: H2 as product; NH3 as product; CO2 as reactant; CO as reactant\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: C2H5NO2 + H2CO + HCN + NH3 + H2O -> C3H7NO2 | reactants minus products: C+1, H+6, N+2, O+2 | balanceable if adding: CO2 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: C3H6O + NH3 -> C3H7NO2 | reactants minus products: H+2, O-1 | no single common small species (H2O, H2, NH3, CO2, ...) fixes it\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: C3H6O + NH3 + H2 -> C3H7NO + H2O | reactants minus products: H+2, O-1 | b